'''''DC's Stargirl''''', or simply '''''Stargirl''''', is an American [[Superhero fiction|superhero]] television series created by [[Geoff Johns]] that premiered on streaming service [[DC Universe (streaming service)|DC Universe]]. It is based on the [[DC Comics]] [[superhero]] [[Courtney Whitmore]], created by Johns and Lee Moder. The series follows high school student Courtney Whitmore who discovers the cosmic staff originally wielded by [[Sylvester Pemberton|Starman]] and becomes the inspiration for a new generation of superheroes who become the new incarnation of the [[Justice Society of America]].

DC Universe ordered the series in July 2018. [[Brec Bassinger]] was cast as Courtney Whitmore that September, with additional castings for her family members, the Justice Society of America, and the [[Injustice Society|Injustice Society of America]] through February 2019. Filming for the series began in March 2019 in the Atlanta metropolitan area. ''Stargirl'' premiered on DC Universe on May 18, 2020; the first season consists of 13 episodes and also aired the following day on the broadcast network [[The CW]]. The second season, subtitled ''Summer School'' premiered on August 10, 2021, exclusively on The CW. The third and final season, subtitled ''Frenemies'' premiered on August 31, 2022.<ref name="august">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-walker-all-american-stargirl-1234848285/|title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates, Plus a Late-Summer Return for ''Stargirl''|work=TVLine.com|access-date=July 5, 2022|author=Mitovich, Matt Webb|date=July 5, 2022}}</ref><ref name="Campione">{{cite web|last=Campione|first=Katie|title=''DC's Stargirl'' Will End After Season 3 At The CW|url=https://deadline.com/2022/10/dcs-stargirl-canceled-the-cw-1235158715/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=October 31, 2022|date=October 31, 2022}}</ref>

Ahead of the series premiere, characters from the series were featured in a [[Cameo appearance|cameo]] during the [[Arrowverse]] crossover "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" through archive footage. It established ''Stargirl'' as existing on [[Earth-2 (Arrowverse post-Crisis)|a parallel Earth]] to the Arrowverse. The show has received critical acclaim.
