The following table represents viewership data for each episode's airing on The CW, as DC Universe did not release viewership information.<ref name="VarietyS2Renew" /> The pilot episode was tied for the second-best series debut on The CW for the [[2019–20 United States network television schedule|2019–20 television season]] with ''[[Nancy Drew (2019 TV series)|Nancy Drew]]'' after ''[[Batwoman (TV series)|Batwoman]]'',<ref name="VarietyPilotRatings" /> and was the best summer series premiere on the network since [[Whose Line Is It Anyway? (American season 9)|''Whose Line Is It Anyway?'' season nine]] in 2013.<ref name="THRPilotRatings" /> Through the first seven episodes of the season, ''Stargirl'' was averaging a 0.2 rating for adults 18–49 and close to 1 million initial viewers per episode, which was "on par" with The CW's [[Arrowverse]] series.<ref name="VarietyS2Renew" />

