===Critical response===
On [[Rotten Tomatoes]], the first season has an approval rating of 89% based on 38 reviews, with an average rating of 7.61/10. The website's critical consensus reads: "A stellar series perfect for anyone looking for a little hope, ''Stargirl'' is delightful fun the whole family can enjoy".<ref>{{Cite Rotten Tomatoes |id=stargirl |type=tv |season=1 |title=Stargirl |access-date=September 22, 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref> On [[Metacritic]] it has a weighted average score of 68 out of 100 based on 8 reviews, indicating "generally favorable reviews".<ref>{{Cite Metacritic|id=dcs-stargirl|type=tv |season=1 |title=Stargirl|access-date=August 9, 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

Brian Lowry of [[CNN]] described the series as "hardly seeks to reinvent the wheel, or even expand the mold. Still, its mix of solid characters, clever writing and youthful exuberance casts a brighter light than most".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/18/entertainment/stargirl-review/index.html|title='Stargirl' brings a lighter touch to DC's superhero universe|website=[[CNN]]|first=Brian|last=Lowry|date=May 18, 2020|access-date=August 9, 2020|archive-date=November 15, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115214602/https://www.cnn.com/2020/05/18/entertainment/stargirl-review/index.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Daniel Fienberg of ''[[The Hollywood Reporter]]'' gave a review, calling it "derivative, but should fill the superhero-origin-story-shaped hole in your heart" and wrote: "The result is that a show that is frequently derivative to the point of distraction might actually fill a need for viewers able to concentrate on its occasional charms until better superhero shows return".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/stargirl-review-1295190|title=Stargirl': TV Review|website=The Hollywood Reporter|first=Daniel|last=Fienberg|date=May 19, 2020|access-date=August 9, 2020|archive-date=November 15, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115214535/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/stargirl-review-1295190|url-status=live}}</ref>

On Rotten Tomatoes, the second season holds an approval rating of 100% based on 5 reviews, with an average rating of 8.2/10.<!--The website's critical consensus states, "."--><ref>{{Cite Rotten Tomatoes |id=stargirl |type=tv |season=2 |title=Stargirl |access-date=May 19, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

